{{- define "chart.purpose" -}}
Wrapper chart for CloudNativePG (`0.29.1` / `1.30.1`) and optional `plugin-barman-cloud` (`0.9.0` / `v0.16.0`) on workload clusters. Reconciles PostgreSQL `Cluster`s across all namespaces and publishes a pinned `ClusterImageCatalog` (`postgresql-standard` for PostgreSQL 16, 17, 18).
{{- end -}}

{{- define "chart.whereItRuns" -}}
- **Roles / providers:** `roles: [workload]`, all providers (`namespace: cnpg-system`, `serverSideDiff: true`).
- **Catalog label:** `addons.platform.koorikla.io/cloudnative-pg` (`default: false`, opt-in with `"true"` per cluster via `addons.cloudnative-pg: true`).
{{- end -}}

{{- define "chart.day2Notes" -}}
- CRDs come from the chart (`crds.create`) and are applied server-side (the `Cluster` CRD exceeds the client-side annotation limit). The operator generates its webhook certificate and patches the caBundles itself; `serverSideDiff` keeps those fields out of drift.
- Watch scope is cluster-wide (`config.clusterWide`): ClusterRole `cnpg` covers the Pods (incl. `pods/exec`), PVCs, Services, Secrets, Jobs, PDBs, Roles and PodMonitors of every PostgreSQL cluster. Aggregation to admin/edit/view stays off.
- Images are multi-arch and digest-pinned; the operator image is also the instance manager injected into every PostgreSQL pod. "standard" PostgreSQL images carry no in-tree barman-cloud: backups use the Barman Cloud plugin.
- On-demand Barman backups and restore drills: [backup and restore](../../docs/runbooks/backup-restore.md#6-cloudnativepg-cloudnative-pg).
{{- end -}}

